Synthetic ORCA outputs for the integration tests.

These files are NOT real ORCA runs. They contain only the sections the parser
looks at, in the layout ORCA 5/6 uses, trimmed to a few lines each.  The real
reference output lives in ../sp_uks (ORCA 6.1.0, shortened in the population
analysis and citation blocks only).

  opt_ok        converged optimisation, writes opt_ok.best.xyz
  opt_fail      optimisation hit the cycle limit
  freq_ts       UKS frequency job with one imaginary mode + thermochemistry
  numfreq       same as freq_ts but numerical frequencies: no CP-SCF in the output
  optfreq_min   opt + freq, minimum
  nics          NMR with two ghost atoms (NICS)
  fod           FOD single point (N_FOD)
  scan          relaxed surface scan, three steps
  tddft         two excited states, Davidson converged
  scf_fail      SCF not converged, error termination
  notfully      "Wavefunction not fully converged" (accepted only with -ncf)
  incomplete    truncated output (job killed or still running)
  empty         zero-byte .out
  missing       no .out at all
  garbage       .out with no ORCA content
  input_error   unrecognised keyword
  spincont      large <S**2> deviation (warning)
